  "_about": "Services a domain's DNS TXT records show it uses, beyond the verification tokens the DNS-SD plugin already records as verified_for relationships. A mail sender must be named in the domain's SPF record, so an SPF domain matches an include: or redirect= mechanism of a v=spf1 record when the mechanism's domain is that domain or ends with it. Every SPF domain is the value the vendor's own documentation tells customers to publish, cited in source; an entry that cannot be confirmed there does not belong here. verification_markers find TXT records that look like a service's verification token (the text before the first '=' or ':' contains a marker); those no DNS-SD prefix recognizes, and SPF includes no entry here matches, are reported as unrecognized so this file and the DNS-SD prefixes can grow from enumerated data. A token or include can outlive the service, so these are evidence of use, not proof of a current contract. Add vendors here, not in Go code.",
